[E0414] Error: `seen` was read while `note`, which writes it, is still used
    ╭─[ err/541_a_writing_closure_holds_what_it_writes/main.wip:12:17 ]
    │
  7 │     val note = (x: i64) => {
    │         ──┬─
    │           ╰─── `note` writes `seen`
    │
 12 │     val early = seen
    │                 ──┬─
    │                   ╰─── `seen` read here
 13 │     note(2)
    │     ──┬─
    │       ╰─── `note` used here, after
    │
    │ Help: use `seen` after the last use of `note`, or give it to `note` as an argument
    │
    │ Note: a closure kept in a `val` that writes what it captures holds it as a `&var` is held, until the closure's last use: nothing else reads or changes it before then
────╯
